Tree Warden - Gypsy Moth Superintendent		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Since the late 1890s, all cities and towns in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts must have a Tree Warden to care for trees on public property, as stipulated in our General Laws. The Tree Warden is responsible for the care and control of all public shade trees except those within a state highway and those in public parks or open places under the jurisdiction of the Park Commissioners. If you have concerns relating to public shade trees in any way, please contact the Tree Warden. 
     

 
